Press patch 0005: dependency pins that install on Python 3.14 next to Frappe 16.
wrapt ~=1.15.0 stays: 1.15.0 installs from its pure Python wheel (py3-none-any), so no C build; only slower (review 1, minor 4).
Purpose: keep pyproject.toml truthful for the locked image, so "uv pip check" can pass.
  ansible 3.4.0 -> 14.6.0      ansible-base 2.10 cannot import on Python 3.12+ (decision 0018)
  oci 2.180.0 -> 2.192.0       2.180.0 needs cryptography<47; Frappe 16 pins cryptography 50
  pexpect 4.8.0 -> 4.9.0       Frappe 16 pins 4.9.0
  pyOpenSSL ~=23.2 -> ~=26.4   Frappe 16 pins 26.4
  python-telegram-bot removed  cannot import on Python 3.12+ (patch 0004)
  requests <2.32 -> ~=2.33     Frappe 16 pins 2.33
  sql_metadata 2.10 -> ~=3.0.1 Frappe 16 pins 3.0.1
  stripe ~=2.56 -> 3.1.0       2.56 vendors six 1.x, which cannot import on Python 3.12+ (decision 0019)
  playwright 1.49.1 -> 1.65.2  1.49.1 pins greenlet 3.1.1, which has no Python 3.14 build
  semgrep 1.159.0 -> 1.79.0    1.159.0 pins opentelemetry-api <1.38; Frappe 16 pins 1.45. 1.79.0 is
                               the newest semgrep that resolves; the marketplace audit is not tested
  frappe-mcp pinned to a commit  the unpinned Git URL was not reproducible
  dnspython 1.16.0 -> 2.9.2    CVE-2023-29483 and two later DoS fixes; Resolver.query still exists
  paramiko 3.3.1 -> 5.1.0      Terrapin (CVE-2023-48795) and SHA-1 RSA (CVE-2026-44405); Press
                               code does not import paramiko (Ansible plugins and docker ssh do)
  setuptools 80.9.0 -> 84.2.1  CVE-2026-59890 and GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w; 84 has no pkg_resources,
                               every import of it in the image is guarded by try/except
  The three upgrades come from the OSV scan of the lock (review 1, finding 3).
Upstream: proposal 4 in backend/docs/press-python314-upstream.md.
Remove when Press ships Python 3.14 pins (decision O-52 in backend/PROJECT-RECORD.md).

